          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Apart from medication, what helps with long-term insomnia?",
          "answer": "To help manage long-term insomnia without medication, focusing on a consistent sleep schedule is key. The most important adjustment is to maintain a consistent wake time, even on weekends. This is because your body's internal clock, which regulates sleep timing, is strongly influenced by morning light. While your bedtime can be flexible, keeping your wake time the same helps to set this clock.\n\nThese sleep habits are supportive measures. They complement other treatments for chronic insomnia rather than replacing them entirely.\n\n(Source: lifestyle-insomnia-sleep)\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
